      "side": 1,
      "message": "A long story..\n\nThis is a kernel driver bug, kernel controls kb backlight by EC_CMD_PWM_SET_DUTY, instead of using the expected command EC_CMD_PWM_SET_KEYBOARD_BACKLIGHT.\n\nEC_CMD_PWM_SET_DUTY handler does not control GPIO_EN_KEYBOARD_BACKLIGHT correctly. \nThe only way to turn on GPIO_EN_KEYBOARD_BACKLIGHT is in HOOK_RESUME and current_percent is not zero. (this is what the commit message trying to say).\n\nIf you are in S0 and toggles kb backlight from off to on, EC_CMD_PWM_SET_DUTY won\u0027t enable GPIO_EN_KEYBOARD_BACKLIGHT for you.",
